# out of points, confronted — an attempt costs a point, and with none left the box says RUNAWAY
#
# Carrying an act out costs a point like looking and thinking do, and there is none to carry one out
# without: a pool of 3 buys exactly one chain — a look, a thought, the attempt. A success hands the
# pool back; a failure does not. Here the failure is also heard: the wolf comes to the noise and
# stands over the member, who can then neither look, think nor act. The box that says so names who
# bars the way and its button is RUNAWAY, the roll it always was.
#
# Examine's whole failure table is the thread lost, which cannot take hold with no point left, so
# the failure costs the attempt's point and nothing more.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Crown" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Giant Tree" --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal examine
advance 12 180

click observe "Test Giant Tree"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Giant Tree"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180

# --- one point left: the act is offered ---
expect-state noetic points=1/3
expect-state where out_of_points=no
expect-state symbols click act 0
expect-no-state symbols (disabled) click act

# --- the attempt costs it, and failing gives nothing back ---
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb examine
expect-state noetic points=0/3

# --- the wolf heard it: confronted, with nothing to answer it with ---
expect-state where confronted=Enemy:wolf exit=RUNAWAY out_of_points=yes
expect NO NOETIC POINT LEFT
expect wolf stands in the way
expect [ RUNAWAY ]
expect-not [ LEAVE ]

# --- the wolf is on the map already observed, and cannot be thought about: that costs a point ---
expect-state trees element "the wolf"
expect-state symbols click think "the wolf" (disabled)

# --- its button is the runaway's roll ---
strategy succeed
click exit
wait
click continue
advance 12 180
wait mode WorldView 60
quit
